From 5cbebd018ba10428c6db57e00de6c7c24dd7fab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aryan Randeriya <aryan.k.randeriya@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 17:51:16 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/18] fix(scripts): run inserted and timer-string scripts as
 their own V8 scripts

Dynamically inserted scripts (fetched and inline) and setTimeout/setInterval
string handlers ran through `(0, eval)(body)` in bootstrap.js. Their stacks
therefore read `eval at execute (<obscura:bootstrap>:371:28), <anonymous>:2:7`
instead of the script URL, which exposes the engine and loses the source.
Cloudflare Turnstile collects such stacks from its api.js.

- New op_script_run_classic compiles the source with v8::Script::compile and a
  ScriptOrigin naming the script URL, in the realm named by the caller's frame
  id, so top-level var/function still become globals of that realm.
- A fetched script is queued as a native microtask of the op itself, so no
  bootstrap frame sits below its top level. document.currentScript is set and
  restored by before/done callbacks inside the same call.
- Inline inserted scripts are named by the document (base) URL, as parser
  inline scripts already were; string timers get no URL (<anonymous>).
- Frame document scripts were compiled with no origin at all; they now carry
  their URL (the frame document URL for inline ones).
- Uncaught exceptions from page scripts, including SyntaxErrors, are now
  reported to window.onerror and error listeners with message, URL, line and
  column. Before, parser-script errors only reached the host log. ErrorEvent
  gains filename, lineno and colno.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
